# Git and pull requests

- One concern per branch and PR. Name branches `chore/…`, `fix/…`, `feat/…`, `docs/…` from the topic, not a catch-all (`post-frontend` is the anti-pattern).
- Branch from up-to-date `main`. Do not pile a tooling change onto an unrelated feature branch.
- Commit only when the user asks. Message says why, not a file dump.
- Do not amend pushed commits, force-push `main`, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not delete old feature branches after merge. Leave them as historical refs; the user retires them.
- Do not rewrite README, app code, and Cursor config in the same PR unless the user asked for that mix.
- Before opening a PR: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and tests for the touched area.
- Bugbot reviews GitHub PRs after the user enables the repo in Cursor Automations. Do not assume Bugbot is on.
